From 512a87d1b86876f737c2c5a59a6ef106b1a9c096 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <port@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:36:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] 0017: enter the accelerator path with boot-args alone

The fire path needs a Mac-built userspace binary, so every Navi 44 boot
logs "ARMED (not fired)" and stops: LoadAccelerator is published only
from accelExperiment()'s fire branch, and nothing on this PC can issue
the verb. Add navi48-accel-fire-at-boot, gated by a pure decision that
refuses rather than calls when the ladder never ran or stage 17 did not
pass - the fire path installs the TTL hook before its own exposure gate
can withhold the property, so an unattended boot loop is the failure
mode being protected against.
---
